    "type": "question",
    "label": "16",
    "prompt": "Factorise fully $x^8-1$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\begin{gathered}(x-1)(x+1)(x^2+1)\\\\{}\\times(x^2-\\sqrt2x+1)(x^2+\\sqrt2x+1)\\end{gathered}$\n\nUse difference of squares repeatedly, with\n\n$x^4+1=(x^2+1)^2-(\\sqrt2x)^2$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^8-1&=(x^4-1)(x^4+1)\\\\x^8-1&=(x^2-1)(x^2+1)(x^4+1)\\\\x^8-1&=(x-1)(x+1)(x^2+1)(x^4+1)\\\\x^8-1&=(x-1)(x+1)(x^2+1)\\big[(x^2+1)^2-(\\sqrt2x)^2\\big]\\\\x^8-1&=(x-1)(x+1)(x^2+1)(x^2-\\sqrt2x+1)(x^2+\\sqrt2x+1).\\end{align*}$$\nThis is fully factorised over the reals: $x^2+1>0$ and $x^2\\pm\\sqrt2x+1=(x\\pm\\frac{1}{\\sqrt2})^2+\\frac{1}{2}>0$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
